From f3d6ac02be148321b8a502463fa0deb2fa298a7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:29:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cp,os: C versions of context save/restore and divider/sqrt
 hooks (SDK_PORT_3DS)

Four MWCC asm functions and the software divider and square-root hooks, under
SDK_PORT_3DS. The DS text is unchanged: gcc -E -P of each file without
SDK_PORT_3DS equals the file before this patch, for -DSDK_ARM9 and for
-DSDK_ARM7 (lib/NitroSDK is built for ARM9 only, config.mk; the ARM7 run is extra).
Every #else branch is the original text.

CP_SaveContext (cp/CP_context.c; asm at the original lines 4-24)
  DS/MWCC: reads DIV_NUMER and DIV_DENOM (one 16-byte block at 0x290),
  DIVCNT (0x280) masked with #3, SQRT_PARAM (0x2B8), SQRTCNT (0x2B0) masked
  with #1. Stores div_numer@0, div_denom@8, sqrt@16, div_mode@24 (u16),
  sqrt_mode@26 (u16); the padding at 28-31 is not written.
  Platinum 0006 (cp_context.c hunk): the same reads and the same masks, through
  REG_CP_DIVCNT_MODE_MASK and REG_CP_SQRTCNT_MODE_MASK (0x3 and 0x1 in
  io_reg.h, the same values as the asm). Differences: Platinum guards with
  SDK_CW/__MWERKS__ and this patch uses SDK_PORT_3DS, and the read order here
  is the asm's (numer, denom, DIVCNT, SQRT_PARAM, SQRTCNT).
  Port: port_thread.c HandOver (line 203) calls it when a thread is switched away.

CPi_RestoreContext (cp/CP_context.c; asm at the original lines 26-47)
  DS/MWCC: writes DIV_NUMER and DIV_DENOM, then DIVCNT = div_mode (strh, not
  masked), SQRTCNT = sqrt_mode, SQRT_PARAM = sqrt. The writes are in that order.
  Here: the same five writes in the same order, then CPi_PortUpdateDiv() and
  CPi_PortUpdateSqrt() once each. Platinum 0006 calls CPi_PORT_DIV_WRITTEN() and
  CPi_PORT_SQRT_WRITTEN() (macros that patch 0002 adds to divider.h and sqrt.h).
  HGSS has neither header, so the two port functions are declared here with a
  local extern under SDK_PORT_3DS. Both hooks run after all five writes, as on
  Platinum.
  Port: port_thread.c HandOver (line 228) calls it when a thread is resumed.

OS_InitContext (os/os_context.c; asm at the original lines 4-39)
  DS/MWCC: stores PC+4; with SDK_CONTEXT_HAS_SP_SVC (defined by os/context.h)
  stores SP_SVC = newsp, then SP = newsp - HW_SVC_STACK_SIZE; SP -= 4 when bit
  2 of SP is set (tst #4); CPSR = SYS mode | THUMB if bit 0 of the entry is
  set, else SYS mode | ARM; r0-r12 and lr zeroed. SP (r13) and the coprocessor
  context are not written.
  Here: the same fields with the same values. Platinum 0006 does the same.
  Port: os_thread.c:295 and :319 pass the entry and the stack. port_thread.c
  RunFresh reads pc_plus4, r[0] and lr.

OS_SaveContext (os/os_context.c; asm at the original lines 41-68)
  DS/MWCC: on ARM9 calls CP_SaveContext on context+72; stores CPSR, the SVC SP
  and r0-r14, and PC+4 (the resume point); returns 0. A context resumed by
  OS_LoadContext returns 1 from there.
  Here: returns NitroPort_SaveContext(context), which is FALSE
  (port_thread.c:265). Platinum 0006 does the same.
  Difference from the asm: no CP_SaveContext call. The port saves the CP state
  and CPSR per thread in HandOver at switch time (port_thread.c:203, 205), so a
  save here would be a second copy. The coprocessor state is captured at switch
  time, not at this call. The scheduler does no coprocessor work in between.
  Difference: the OSContext register fields (r0-r14, CPSR, SP_SVC) are not
  written. The port keeps the switched-away thread's CPSR in PortThread.cpsr.

OS_LoadContext (os/os_context.c; asm at the original lines 70-96)
  DS/MWCC: on ARM9 calls CPi_RestoreContext, then sets SVC mode, sets SPSR from
  the saved CPSR, loads the saved registers and jumps to PC+4-4. It does not
  return to its caller.
  Here: NitroPort_LoadContext(context) (port_thread.c:273). It returns when the
  caller is switched back to, which is the port's design (port_thread.c header).
  Difference from the asm: no CPi_RestoreContext before the switch. HandOver
  restores the coprocessor state of the thread it resumes (port_thread.c:228).
  A restore here would overwrite the running thread's state before HandOver
  saves it. The Tests paragraph lists the mutation that checks this.

Software divider and square-root hooks (fx/fx_cp.c)
  CPi_PortUpdateDiv() runs once after the last register write that starts a
  division: FX_InvAsync (DIV_DENOM, original line 52), FX_DivAsync (line 63),
  FX_DivS32 and FX_ModS32 (line 69 and 77, before the busy-wait loop).
  CPi_PortUpdateSqrt() runs once after SQRT_PARAM in FX_Sqrt (line 32), before
  FX_GetSqrtResult. Platinum 0002 calls its hooks after every register write.
  Here the port recomputes from the registers, so one call after the sequence
  is enough, and no result is computed from half-written operands.
  Not hooked by this patch (callers found, left for the lead): fx_vec.c,
  fx_vec_mult_add.c, fx_vec_normalize.c, fx_mtx44_ortho.c, fx_mtx44_perspective.c,
  tp.c, src/battle/battle_command.c (CP_SetSqrt*).

Tests: tests/sdk/cp_context/run.sh (the port repo). It builds these three files
with the survey tool's flags and runs them against stub port functions, with
the I/O page mapped at 0x04000000. OS_InitContext is checked field by field
for ARM and Thumb entries and SP with and without bit 2 set; save and restore
are checked against the register values and the padding; the hooks are counted
and checked for the register values they see. Mutation checks: dropping the SP
alignment, the DIVCNT mask, the sqrt hook, a CP restore in OS_LoadContext, and
the FX_DivAsync hook each make the run fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cp/CP_context.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/fx/fx_cp.c      | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++
 src/os/os_context.c | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 108 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cp/CP_context.c b/src/cp/CP_context.c
index e8aecb8..cd77f15 100644
--- a/src/cp/CP_context.c
+++ b/src/cp/CP_context.c
@@ -1,6 +1,36 @@
 #include <nitro.h>
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+/* 3DS port: the software divider and square root (3ds_port/nitro/src/port_cp.c) work out
+ * their result registers from the operands in the registers. Platinum declares these in its
+ * divider.h and sqrt.h (patch 0002); HGSS has neither header, so they are declared here. */
+extern void CPi_PortUpdateDiv(void);
+extern void CPi_PortUpdateSqrt(void);
+
+/* Same register reads and writes, in the same order, as the asm in the #else branch. */
+void CP_SaveContext(CPContext *context)
+{
+    context->div_numer = reg_CP_DIV_NUMER;
+    context->div_denom = reg_CP_DIV_DENOM;
+    context->div_mode = (u16)(reg_CP_DIVCNT & REG_CP_DIVCNT_MODE_MASK);     /* and r12, r12, #3 */
+    context->sqrt = reg_CP_SQRT_PARAM;
+    context->sqrt_mode = (u16)(reg_CP_SQRTCNT & REG_CP_SQRTCNT_MODE_MASK);  /* and r2, r2, #1 */
+}
+
+void CPi_RestoreContext(CPContext *context)
+{
+    reg_CP_DIV_NUMER = context->div_numer;
+    reg_CP_DIV_DENOM = context->div_denom;
+    reg_CP_DIVCNT = context->div_mode;      /* strh, the mode as stored (not masked) */
+    reg_CP_SQRTCNT = context->sqrt_mode;
+    reg_CP_SQRT_PARAM = context->sqrt;
+
+    /* Both units restart from the registers just written. */
+    CPi_PortUpdateDiv();
+    CPi_PortUpdateSqrt();
+}
+#else
 asm void CP_SaveContext(register CPContext *context)
 {
     ldr r1, =REG_DIV_NUMER_ADDR
@@ -45,3 +75,4 @@ asm void CPi_RestoreContext(register CPContext *context)
 
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
diff --git a/src/fx/fx_cp.c b/src/fx/fx_cp.c
index 21ea10c..4dd0154 100644
--- a/src/fx/fx_cp.c
+++ b/src/fx/fx_cp.c
@@ -10,6 +10,15 @@ fx32 FX_GetSqrtResult(void);
 void FX_InvAsync(fx32 x);
 void FX_DivAsync(fx32 numerator, fx32 denominator);
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+/* 3DS port: no divider or square-root unit. These work out the result registers from the operands
+ * just written (3ds_port/nitro/src/port_cp.c). Each is called once after a sequence of writes that
+ * starts an operation, before anything reads the result. Platinum declares them in its divider.h
+ * and sqrt.h (patch 0002); HGSS has neither header. */
+extern void CPi_PortUpdateDiv(void);
+extern void CPi_PortUpdateSqrt(void);
+#endif
+
 fx32 FX_Div(fx32 numerator, fx32 denominator) {
     FX_DivAsync(numerator, denominator);
     return FX_GetDivResult();
@@ -30,6 +39,9 @@ fx32 FX_Sqrt(fx32 x) {
     if (x > 0) {
         reg_CP_SQRTCNT = 0x1;
         reg_CP_SQRT_PARAM = (u64)((fx64)x << 32);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+        CPi_PortUpdateSqrt();
+#endif
         return FX_GetSqrtResult();
     } else {
         return 0;
@@ -50,6 +62,9 @@ void FX_InvAsync(fx32 x) {
     reg_CP_DIVCNT = 0x1;
     reg_CP_DIV_NUMER = (fx64)0x00001000 << 32;
     reg_CP_DIV_DENOM = (u32)x;
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CPi_PortUpdateDiv();
+#endif
 }
 
 fx32 FX_GetSqrtResult() {
@@ -61,12 +76,18 @@ void FX_DivAsync(fx32 numerator, fx32 denominator) {
     reg_CP_DIVCNT = 0x1;
     reg_CP_DIV_NUMER = (u64)((fx64)numerator << 32);
     reg_CP_DIV_DENOM = (u32)denominator;
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CPi_PortUpdateDiv();
+#endif
 }
 
 fx32 FX_DivS32(fx32 numerator, fx32 denominator) {
     reg_CP_DIVCNT = 0x0;
     *(REGType32v *)&reg_CP_DIV_NUMER = (u32)numerator; // 32bit write for some reason
     reg_CP_DIV_DENOM = (u32)denominator;
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CPi_PortUpdateDiv();
+#endif
     while (reg_CP_DIVCNT & REG_CP_DIVCNT_BUSY_MASK) {}
     return (fx32)(*(REGType32v *)&reg_CP_DIV_RESULT);
 }
@@ -75,6 +96,9 @@ fx32 FX_ModS32(fx32 num, fx32 mod) {
     reg_CP_DIVCNT = 0x0;
     *(REGType32v *)&reg_CP_DIV_NUMER = (u32)num; // 32bit write for some reason
     reg_CP_DIV_DENOM = (u32)mod;
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    CPi_PortUpdateDiv();
+#endif
     while (reg_CP_DIVCNT & REG_CP_DIVCNT_BUSY_MASK) {}
     return (fx32)(*(REGType32v *)&reg_CP_DIVREM_RESULT);
 }
diff --git a/src/os/os_context.c b/src/os/os_context.c
index 0c71371..30abaed 100644
--- a/src/os/os_context.c
+++ b/src/os/os_context.c
@@ -1,6 +1,58 @@
 #include <nitro/os/context.h>
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+/* 3DS port: the port switches threads (3ds_port/nitro/src/port_thread.c). */
+BOOL NitroPort_SaveContext(void *context);
+void NitroPort_LoadContext(void *context);
+
+/* The same fields as the asm in the #else branch: PC+4; SP_SVC (the SP the context
+ * came in with) and SP below the SVC stack reserve, 8-byte aligned; CPSR for system mode,
+ * Thumb if the entry address is odd; r0-r12 and lr zeroed. SP (r13) and the coprocessor
+ * context are not written here, as in the asm. */
+void OS_InitContext(OSContext *context, u32 newpc, u32 newsp)
+{
+    context->pc_plus4 = newpc + 4;
+
+#ifdef SDK_CONTEXT_HAS_SP_SVC
+    context->sp_svc = newsp;
+    newsp -= HW_SVC_STACK_SIZE;
+#endif
+
+    if (newsp & 4) {
+        newsp -= 4;
+    }
+    context->sp = newsp;
+
+    context->cpsr = (newpc & 1) ? (HW_PSR_SYS_MODE | HW_PSR_THUMB_STATE)
+                                : (HW_PSR_SYS_MODE | HW_PSR_ARM_STATE);
+
+    {
+        int i;
+        for (i = 0; i < 13; i++) {
+            context->r[i] = 0;
+        }
+    }
+    context->lr = 0;
+}
+
+/* FALSE: "saved, now switch". The port records which machine thread plays this context.
+ * When the thread is resumed, OS_LoadContext returns in it, which is where the asm's
+ * "resumed" return value 1 would have come back. The CPU and coprocessor state of the
+ * switched-away thread is saved by the port at switch time (port_thread.c, HandOver). */
+BOOL OS_SaveContext(OSContext *context)
+{
+    return NitroPort_SaveContext(context);
+}
+
+/* Returns when the caller is switched back to (see OS_SaveContext). The coprocessor state of the
+ * thread that is resumed is restored by the port at switch time (HandOver), not here: restoring
+ * it before the switch would overwrite the running thread's coprocessor state before it is saved. */
+void OS_LoadContext(OSContext *context)
+{
+    NitroPort_LoadContext(context);
+}
+#else
 asm void OS_InitContext(register OSContext *context, register u32 newpc, register u32 newsp) {
     add newpc, newpc, #4
     str newpc, [context, #OS_CONTEXT_PC_PLUS4]
@@ -94,3 +146,4 @@ asm void OS_LoadContext(register OSContext *context) {
 
     subs pc, lr, #4
 }
+#endif
-- 
2.43.0

